    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d238">

                <pb facs="0513" n="443" sameAs="frus:frus1883/pg443"/>

                <head>No. 238.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Frelinghuysen to Mr. Lowell.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1883-07-18"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 18,
                        1883</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 634.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to the instruction No. 562,
                    of the 31st of March last, of this Department to you concerning the Venezuela
                    debts, I now inclose<anchor n="*" xml:id="d238-f1"/> herewith for your
                    information a copy of a note from Count Hatzfeldt, the minister of foreign
                    affairs of Germany, in which he states that the imperial German Government will
                    ageer to whatever the other nations interested approve, with due regard to its
                    treaty rights.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>FEED’K T. FRELINGHUYSEN.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d238-f1" n="*" xml:id="d238-f1-content">
                <p>For inclosure see inclosure to document No. 203, under Germany, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">ante.</hi></p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
